    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29736" root="عفر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَعُوا فِى عَافُورِ شَرٍّ</span></b> , (S, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرٍّ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى عَفَارِ</span></b> ,
(TA,) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى عَاثُورِ شَرٍّ</span>, (Fr, S, K,) i. e., <i>They
fell into difficulty,</i> or <i>distress.</i> (S.) Some say
that the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ف</span> is substituted for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ث</span>. (TA.) [But
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عاثور</span>.]

